# QUESTION: When a reload changes bus hub server central certificate to
# fleet-hub on a serving hub, does a verifying client anchored on fleet-hub's
# CA connect while an already-connected client stays up with connected-since unchanged?
# WHY NOT A UNIT TEST: proves non-vacuous live TLS certificate rotation across
# three real daemons (hub plus two verifying clients with distinct CAs).
# VALIDATES: fleet-1 AC-38, A-12.
option=timeout:value=240s
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture managed/fleet-reload-certificate-rotated $PORT $PORT2 $PORT3:timeout=240s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: reload rotated managed certificate for new handshakes while keeping existing session
